# promise: #413
# An incognito window's pages all load in one off-the-record context, so its space header's menu
# offers no Set Profile (the checkmark moved and nothing changed), and none of what the window's
# Spaces menu turns off there: Export into Folder, Manage Spaces…, Delete Space
# (GitHub #413). A normal window's header keeps Arc's whole menu.
budget rss=700 stalls50=10
seed settings.json {"toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "showToolbar": false}
from://open?url=${PAGE}?n=normal
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
wait 1
from://debug?spaceMenu=normal
expect-log space menu normal: Rename Space…\|Edit Theme Color…\|Set Profile ▸\|Search Engine ▸\|──\|New Folder[^|]*\|──\|Export .*\|Delete Space$
from://action/newIncognitoWindow
wait 2
from://debug?spaceMenu=incognito&window=incognito
expect-log space menu incognito: Rename Space…\|Edit Theme Color…\|Search Engine ▸\|──\|New Folder[^|]*$
